{"ts":"2026-11-12T17:47:34.930Z","actor":"claude","stage":"factcheck","action":"factcheck.review","details":{"verdict":"pass","notes":"Rebuilt with laps + journey scenes. Speed: 'Light travels 299,792 km every second' (light-speed); 'about seven and a half times around the Earth, every second' and on-screen '7.5× around Earth, every second' = 299,792.458 / (2π·6,378.137 km = 40,075 km) = 7.48 (earth-laps, NASA Earth Fact Sheet); laps drawn slowed down and labelled 'Shown slowed down'; Earth is the real Apollo 17 photo (asset earth-apollo17, NASA/JSC, credited on screen). Distance journey: Sun→Earth to scale (1 of 5.2 AU), Earth sub '150 million km' (sun-distance), clock 0 → 8.3333 min printed '8 min 20 s' = arrival badge (sun-light-time); 'But space is enormous' is framing, no claim. Jupiter journey: same photon continues Earth→Jupiter, clock 8 min 20 s → 43 min (jupiter-light-time: 5.2 AU, 43 min); 'The same light keeps going' is literally what is drawn (light from the Sun passing Earth's orbit). Jupiter sub '5.2 AU on average' ✓. Compare and outro unchanged."},"gitSha":"56e31e5"}
